  "task": {
    "objective": "A three-person crew must collect three fragile survey capsules from marked river buoys and bank them at its home berth. The skiff retains velocity until counter-thrust or braking changes it. Walking crew, filled corner tanks and loaded capsules change its balance; loose capsules slide toward the low edge and can be lost. Two reusable clips can secure capsules, while cliffs, reef collision and severe imbalance damage the hull.",
    "natural_termination": "Hull exhaustion, then any capsule lost, then all three banked. Otherwise time limit 192. Natural success/failure has priority over horizon.",
    "interaction": "A crew member walks to the upper scoop, moving mass upward; a colleague shifts ballast downward before a capsule can satisfy the loading balance check. A loaded capsule changes torque. The clip worker must reach its current deck cell while the helm keeps the boat stationary or navigates safely; securing it prevents gravity motion but preserves its contribution to torque. A helm command changes persistent velocity. Waiting does not stop travel; a later opposite impulse or brake is necessary before stationary sampling or banking. A periodic current impulse can introduce lateral motion. The crew can read tide phase and centre terrain, but the proper correction depends on existing velocity and available fuel. When two clips are occupied, collecting another capsule requires retaining safe balance, releasing a clip or banking earlier. The reward does not directly prescribe one of those strategies. Walking, filling tanks and moving loose capsules alter a shared torque calculation, so independent locally sensible actions can jointly cause an edge loss or structural damage.",
    "observation_access": "All physical quantities public; only identity one-hot differs by crew. Flat observations have exactly 1939 columns.",
    "action_mask_semantics": "Masks permit attempts whose outcome depends on simultaneous partner/opponent actions. Static bounds/roles/resources are masked; raw transition rules resolve occupancy, new-object availability, adjacency and conflicts. Attempt validity does not guarantee an effect.",
    "reward_definition": {
      "team_reward_formula": "For each active transition, r = newly_banked_count + 2*I(new natural success) - I(new natural failure) - 0.02*hull_units_lost - 0.001. Return [r,r,r] as float32.",
      "natural_failure": "Reason 2 or 3, selected on this transition.",
      "horizon": "A horizon truncation has no invented success/failure bonus; it retains the ordinary bank/damage/step reward of that transition.",
      "accounting": "A capsule can yield a banking reward only on its 1->2 status change. Clips, filling/draining tanks and observations yield no direct reward.",
      "empirical_status": "These are proposed reward rules. No reward values, completion rates or learning results have been observed."
    }
  },
